{
  "description": "A dev project with two data locations, file path settings and session and subject tables. Covers each folder rule (index range, regular expression, function, several levels), the defaults for ids, adapters with and without a built-in equivalent, derived and skipped columns, rows without a key and duplicates, and notes: on kept, duplicate and left-out rows, without a time, of an unknown type, and two in the same second; and a filtered table, which becomes a view (one of its rows is not in the master table); dev's pipelines, with the tasks that have a method here and their rules for new sessions. The project's own session methods (code/+RatNav/+sessionmethod) become methods of sessions that run dev's code (their files copied into matlab/, in the same packages), with the options read from their text; a file that is not a session method is left out, and a pipeline task that calls one of them becomes a step. Its own file adapters (code/+RatNav/+fileadapter: a class and a function-based one) become legacy file adapters with their code copied, and the variables read with them data variables; a function there is left out. The option presets users made become presets: NoRMCorre's with dev's options mapped to the module method's, the session methods' as they are, renamed when called default, with an option that does not fit left out; dev's default preset becomes the preferred one; those of methods not here, or of dev's options with no equivalent, are named. The queued tasks become tasks on hold in dev's order, with dev's options over their preset's, less those not here, not queueable, of sessions not here or naming none; the completed tasks of the history and the finished tasks of the Progress column go into the run journal, and the column's pipeline into core.pipeline. dev's app preferences give the settings.",
